Running the tests
=================

The suite runs against a **pristine Redmine** — never against a customised
image — so that it tests the plugin, not a host application's patches.

Locally, everything is driven from Docker:

    script/test-docker.sh up          # pristine redmine + mysql, prepared (first run)
    script/test-docker.sh run         # unit + functional suite
    script/test-docker.sh run test/unit/ldap_setting_test.rb
    script/test-docker.sh run test/unit/ldap_setting_test.rb:42
    script/test-docker.sh shell       # poke around inside
    script/test-docker.sh down        # clean up

The plugin working tree is bind-mounted, so edits need no rebuild — just re-run.
Override the versions under test with REDMINE_VERSION / MYSQL_VERSION.

Inside an already-prepared Redmine environment (a CI runner, or the container
above) the two halves can be used directly:

    script/test-setup.sh              # slapd + gems + database + migrations
    script/test-run.sh [test path…]

The default run is unit + functional. The browser tests under test/ui are opt-in,
because they need chromium:

    WITH_BROWSER=1 script/test-setup.sh    # adds chromium + chromium-driver
    script/test-run.sh test/ui

script/test-docker.sh passes WITH_BROWSER through, so `WITH_BROWSER=1
script/test-docker.sh up` prepares a container that can run them.

They build on Redmine's own ApplicationSystemTestCase (Selenium + Chrome), so
log_user and wait_for_ajax come for free. Two things worth knowing before editing
them:

* **ApplicationSystemTestCase#setup calls `Setting.delete_all`**, which throws away
  this plugin's configuration — an LdapSetting lives in
  `Setting.plugin_redmine_ldap_sync`, not in a table of its own. test/ui/base.rb
  assigns it back. Do not reach for `FixtureSet.create_fixtures` to do that: the
  fixture is already in Rails' fixture cache, so the call inserts nothing and
  silently leaves every page rendering an empty, disabled configuration.
* **Fields are addressed by id, buttons by data attribute, not by label.** The
  labels are translated and have been renamed more than once (`account_flags` went
  from "Account flags (user)" to "Lock state attribute"), and a test that fails on
  a reworded label reports a defect that does not exist.


Continuous integration
======================

.github/workflows/test.yml runs the same two scripts against every supported
Redmine (a job per minor version, pristine image as the job container, MySQL as a
service). CI and local runs therefore cannot drift: if it passes here it passes
there, and a failure reproduces with script/test-docker.sh.


The test LDAP directory
=======================

script/test-setup.sh starts a private slapd on localhost:3389 from
test/fixtures/ldap/slapd.conf and seeds it with test/fixtures/ldap/test-ldap.ldif.

slapd must be reachable on **127.0.0.1:3389** specifically: the auth source
fixtures hardcode that address, and they also use 127.0.0.2 as a host that must
*not* answer. A sidecar container therefore does not work — slapd belongs in the
same container/runner as Redmine.

To do it by hand:

    slaptest -f test/fixtures/ldap/slapd.conf -F /etc/ldap/slapd.d/
    chown -R openldap:openldap /etc/ldap/slapd.d /var/lib/ldap
    # restart slapd, then:
    ldapadd -x -D cn=admin,dc=redmine,dc=org -w password \
      -f test/fixtures/ldap/test-ldap.ldif -c


Known issues
============

* One fixture group has a 292-character cn, and its 322-byte DN is rejected by
  the mdb backend (MDB_BAD_VALSIZE on dn2id_add) that replaced hdb in OpenLDAP
  2.5 — the maximum RDN is around 246 bytes. So 29 of the 30 entries load, and
  seeding must use -c or ldapadd stops there and everything after it goes
  missing (which breaks about a dozen tests).

  The entry existed to give Redmine a group name it must refuse (over 255
  characters), exercising the "could not be created" branch. That premise is now
  unreproducible — a name has to exceed 255 characters for Redmine to reject it,
  which is necessarily more bytes than LDAP will accept — so two assertions were
  retargeted: ldap_test_test expects 14 non-dynamic groups, and the branch itself
  is covered by "#sync_users should report groups it could not create", which
  reaches it deterministically with create_groups off.

Coverage
========

COVERAGE=1 writes a simplecov report to coverage/. Off by default so a plain run
neither requires the gem nor writes into the working tree.
